    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249-a2">

                <pb facs="0302" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg268"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 914.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Villiers to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had the honor to receive the note which
                    you were good enough to leave at this office on the 10th instant, conveying
                    proposals from the United States Government for a fresh “modus vivendi,” similar
                    to that of 1891, with regard to seal fisheries in Bering Sea, and for an
                    arrangement for a joint conference of the Powers concerned, to discuss the
                    measures necessary for the preservation of the seals.</p>
                <p>Your communication will receive the immediate consideration of Her Majesty’s
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. H. Villiers.</hi></signed><lb/>(For
                    the Marquis of Salisbury).</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
